'''Jonathan Lowell Spencer "Johnny" Storm''' was a member of the [[Fantastic Four/Void Analyzing Fantastic Four|Fantastic Four]] known as '''Human Torch'''. He was pruned by the [[Time Variance Authority]] and sent to the [[Void]], where he joined the [[Resistance]] opposing [[Cassandra Nova]] and her [[Cassandra Nova's Henchmen|henchmen]]. Human Torch was captured along with [[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]] by a group of Nova's scavengers led by [[Pyro]], who stripped Storm of his powers. When Deadpool openly mentioned Storm's vulgar comments about her, Nova brutally killed him.

==Biography==
===Early Life===
====The Fantastic Four====
Following a mission in space, Johnny Storm gained the power to manipulate and transform his body into fire, which granted him the ability to fly. Along with three others who also possessed unique powers, including [[Mister Fantastic/Void Analyzing Fantastic Four|Reed Richards]], they formed a superhero team known as the [[Fantastic Four/Void Analyzing Fantastic Four|Fantastic Four]], with Storm going by the codename "Human Torch."{{Ref|DW}}

===Banished to the Void===
====Encounter with the TVA====
{{Quote|You're in the [[Void]]. Think of it as purgatory. [[Mister Fantastic/Void Analyzing Fantastic Four|Reed]] called it a metaphysical junkyard where anything useless goes before it gets annihilated forever. And where the [[TVA]] sends people that don't play nice with the rest of the [[Multiverse]]."<br>"Like you?|Human Torch and [[Wolverine]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
At some point, Human Torch had a run in with the [[Multiverse]] which resulted in him being taken by the [[Time Variance Authority]], who pruned him, sending him to the [[Void]], a place that [[Mister Fantastic/Void Analyzing Fantastic Four|Mister Fantastic]] had researched and expressed thoughts on. Human Torch was able to avoid being eaten by [[Alioth]], but others he was with were not so fortunate.{{Ref|DW}}

====Joining the Resistance====
{{Quote|Everyone here's on the run from [[Alioth]]. Most don't make it. There's a [[Resistance]] though. Other people like us that managed to survive. They're hiding out in the borderlands trying to find a way the fuck out of here.|Human Torch to [[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Human Torch came across a group of other heroes who had survived in the [[Void]] from [[Alioth]]. However, the wasteland was ruled by the [[Mutants|mutant]] [[Cassandra Nova]], who forced those trapped in the Void to work for her. This group of heroes, including [[Elektra/Forgotten Elektra|Elektra]], [[Blade/Universe Defender Blade|Blade]], [[Gambit]] and [[X-23]], rebelled against Nova and formed a [[Resistance]], hiding out in the borderlands and trying to figure a way out of the Void. The Resistance spent years in hiding, and any attempt they made to fight Nova only ended in defeat.{{Ref|DW}}

====Meeting Deadpool and Wolverine====
{{Quote|[[Cassandra Nova|She]] might have something to say about that."<br>"Who's 'she'?"<br>"In the [[Void]], you're either food for [[Alioth]] or your work for her.|Human Torch and [[Wolverine]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}} 
When Human Torch went out on a scout mission, he came across [[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]], who were in the middle of [[Duel in the Void|fighting]] each other. Human Torch broke it up by telling them that fighting each other meant that they would lose and warned them that [[Cassandra Nova]]'s [[Cassandra Nova's Henchmen|crew]] was approaching their location. Jumping to the ground, Human Torch revealed himself, which excited Deadpool, who mistook him for a Variant of [[Steve Rogers]].

As they became surrounded by enemies, Human Torch told Deadpool and Wolverine that he would take care of them. [[Pyro]] told Human Torch that there was nowhere for him to run, but he responded that he wasn't planning on running. Human Torch transformed into flame, flew above everyone, and blasted a beam of fire directly at Pyro. However, Pyro was able to stop Human Torch's attack with his own fire-based powers and extinguish all of his fire, rendering him powerless as he fell out of the sky and was knocked unconscious.

Upon being tied up and thrown in a cage with Deadpool and Wolverine to be taken to Nova's [[Cassandra Nova's Compound|compound]], Human Torch explained what the [[Void]] was, using [[Mister Fantastic/Void Analyzing Fantastic Four|Mister Fantastic]]'s explanation to do so. He informed them about [[Alioth]] and the [[Resistance]], so Wolverine thought the Resistance could help them get back to the [[TVA]]. However, Human Torch laughed at the idea, stating that whoever didn't get eaten by Alioth worked for Nova. Human Torch then spent the remainder of the trip expressing his hatred for Nova in extremely vulgar language, which he said he could be quoted on.{{Ref|DW}}

====Death====
{{Quote|I have never said any of those words in my entire life."<br>"Ha! The modesty. People think I'm a shit-talker, but this guy... next level.|Human Torch and [[Deadpool]] to [[Cassandra Nova]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Arriving at the [[Cassandra Nova's Compound|compound]], Human Torch, [[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]] were let out of the cage and brought before [[Cassandra Nova]], who remarked on how she had spent years trying to capture Human Torch.

Deadpool interrupted, revealing to Nova what Human Torch had told them about her, although Human Torch tried to get Deadpool to stop talking at the risk of getting him killed. However, Deadpool continued and repeated exactly what Human Torch said to them verbatim. Human Torch attempted to deny it all, but Deadpool insisted on crediting Human Torch for his words. In a panic, Human Torch feverishly tried to deny insulting Nova, but she coldly used her powers to remove his skin in an instant, killing him.{{Ref|DW}}

===Legacy===
{{Quote|I'm tired of these absolutely vile rumors that I got Johnny killed. Let's take a look at the tape.|[[Deadpool]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
[[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]] were able to [[Escape from Cassandra Nova's Compound|escape]] from [[Cassandra Nova]]'s [[Cassandra Nova's Compound|compound]] when [[Alioth]] arrived, and they later were brought to the [[Resistance Hideout]] by the [[Resistance]]. Deadpool rallied the group to launch an [[Attack on Cassandra Nova's Compound|attack]] on Nova's compound in the hopes of using Nova to finally escape the [[Void]], citing Human Torch's death as a reason. The Resistance was saddened to hear that Human Torch had been murdered, but Wolverine accused Deadpool of getting him killed, which the latter denied.

The attack was successful and Deadpool and Wolverine returned to the former's [[Anchor Being Wolverine|universe]] in time to stop Nova from using the [[Time Ripper]] to destroy all universes but the Void. Returning to the [[Time Variance Authority]] [[Time Variance Authority Office|Office]], Deadpool retrieved and played a tape taken from a hidden camera that was located in his cage. The tape showed Human Torch insulting and demeaning Nova using incredibly crude language, proving that he said the things Deadpool accused him of.{{Ref|DW}}

==Personality==
{{Rewrite}}
{{Quote|[[Cassandra Nova]]. A megalomaniacal, psychotic asshole. A finger-licking, dead inside pixie slab of third-rate dime store nut milk. And I'll tell you what she can do."<br>"I'm listening."<br>"She can lick my god damn cinnamon ring clean and kick rocks all the way to bald hell. In fact, I don't give a shit if she removes all my skin and pops me like some nightmarish blood balloon. If the last thing I do in this godforsaken, cum-gutter existence is light that fuck-box on fire, I still won't die happy!|Johnny Storm and [[Deadpool]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Johnny, much like the [[Steve Rogers|Captain America]] he was mistaken for, was heroic and leaderlike, quickly stopping [[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]]'s fighting to remind them that they only had each other in the [[Void]]. He refused to work for the psychotic [[Cassandra Nova]], becoming a member of the freedom-fighting [[Resistance]] instead. However, he was also sharp-tongued and abrasive, especially about Nova (who he harbored a deep hatred for), using extensive vulgar vocabulary to describe her and his wishes to kill her. Storm was so vulgar and offensive that even Deadpool, who often makes rude remarks, was surprised. Johnny's running his mouth was ultimately his undoing, as Cassandra Nova swiftly killed him after Deadpool repeated the obscenities he had used about her.

==Powers and Abilities==
===Former Powers===
*'''Fire Manipulation''': Johnny had the power to manipulate fire, which formed around his body when he used his abilities. He could channel this fire in the form of blasts and beams.
**'''Flight''': Johnny could use this force to fly, which he did when battling [[Pyro]]. However, Pyro's own ability to manipulate fire negated Johnny's abilities.

