==Trivia==
*In the comics, Johnny Storm is a member of the [[Fantastic Four]] and brother of [[Sue Storm]] with the ability to generate fire throughout his body.

==Behind the Scenes==
*Human Torch in the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]] continues the live-action incarnation of the character from {{WPS|20th Century Fox}}'s {{WPS|Fantastic Four in film#Tim Story films (2005–2007)|''Fantastic Four'' duology}}, who was also portrayed by [[Chris Evans]]; he is the second live-action incarnation of the character, following an incarnation portrayed by {{WPS|Jay Underwood}}.
**Evans agreed to reprise his role following a text from [[Ryan Reynolds (actor)|Ryan Reynolds]] asking if he'd be willing to. Evans later told ''Entertainment Weekly'' that Reynolds may be the only person he'd be willing to reprise the role for.<ref>[https://ew.com/chris-evans-deadpool-and-wolverine-johnny-storm-interview-exclusive-8684326 Chris Evans opens up about ''Deadpool & Wolverine'' role and wearing that suit again (exclusive)]</ref>

